THOUGHT: Annotating the fields as @Nullable didn’t help because NullAway still treats them as needing initialization in this constructor. The remaining option is to ensure they are definitely assigned non-null values along all non-exceptional paths of the constructor. Since these iterator helper objects are cheap and only depend on `this`, I can eagerly initialize them in the constructor after the early loadFactor check and table setup. That will satisfy NullAway without changing behavior (they were previously lazily created). I’ll update the constructor to assign `entries1`, `entries2`, `values1`, `values2`, `keys1`, and `keys2`, then rebuild and confirm the specific error is gone and the total error count remains 453.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '115,117s/^/    /' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/IntFloatMap.java && sed -i '117a\ \ \ \ \ \ \ entries1 = new Entries(this);
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ entries2 = new Entries(this);
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ values1 = new Values(this);
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ values2 = new Values(this);
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ keys1 = new Keys(this);
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ keys2 = new Keys(this);' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/IntFloatMap.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && { echo "IntFloatMap-related errors in new log:"; grep -n "IntFloatMap" new_build_output.log || true; echo "NullAway summary:"; tail -n 40 new_build_output.log | sed -n '/NullAway/,$p'; }
```

